{"ASK_CAR_FUEL","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=friendly,neutral",{"Gas? I siphoned the last of mine two days ago - try the station on the highway","We walked here, there's a tank in the shed, but it's the mower's","Gas? Any gas? I've been looking for days, there's not a drop in the county","No ride, no keys, no gas, no luck, the perfect combination","Siphon it, if you can find a hose and a stomach for it, the taste stays in your mouth for days","I had a truck... ran dry on the way here, left it where it died","Fuel's the new gold, if you find any, you'd better hide it","Try the farms, they keep tanks for tractors, but they guard them with shotguns","I don't drive anymore, I walk, it's slower, but nobody can steal my boots","No idea, I never paid attention to that kind of thing"}},
{"ASK_CAR_FUEL","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=careful",{"Fuel's precious, I'm not telling you where mine is","Why? you want to take my keys?","Go away"}},
